<title>USA: UPS hurt by threat of strike - WSJ.</title>
<headline>UPS hurt by threat of strike - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service of America Inc is laying off employees and losing orders as a Thursday strike deadline looms, The Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Tuesday's electronic edition, the paper said UPS and its Teamsters union have talked for a week without any semblance of an agreement.</p>
<p>Thursday is the final day of the current four-year contract, the paper said, and union members have already given their leadership authorization for a strike.</p>
<p>The company told The Journal that wary customers are diverting deliveries to some UPS rivals.</p>
<p>The company said layoffs had occured but declined to say how many, the paper said.</p>
</text>
